0..66 Comment "/// This source compares composites at stated lambda applications."
67..70 Comment "///"
71..131 Comment "/// `along` applies its stated lambda at each path endpoint."
132..201 Comment "/// A composite can use the lambda reduct or its written application."
202..205 Comment "///"
206..281 Comment "/// The conversion walk substitutes the call argument into the lambda body."
282..338 Comment "/// The kernel checks each composite by its own reading."
339..390 Comment "/// Two composites written apart meet part by part."
391..394 Comment "///"
395..441 Comment "/// - see: #4073 — stated lambda application"
442..477 Comment "/// - see: #4065 — call arguments"
478..521 Comment "/// - see: #3920 — repeated stated lambda"
